EXL3 on the native CUDA engine: TensorFold PR #837 ("cuda: EXL3 linear and grouped routed experts, every codebook and
width, a width per expert", head 224406d7), rebased onto 1.0.12 (46a08c1).

What: hand-written EXL3 kernels for the CUDA engine (exl3_decode.cuh, exl3_linear.cu, exl3_experts.cu), their Zig sides
(cuda/exl3.zig, cuda/exl3_experts.zig, cuda/exl3_upload.zig, core/exl3_load.zig), an `.exl3` arm in qlinear, and their
tests (`tf-cuda-test exl3`). The rebase only resolves list conflicts (kernel tables, core/root.zig, docs) by keeping both
sides, and moves qlinear's `exl3` field above its methods.
Why: TensorFold 1.0.12 has no EXL3 path on CUDA; GLM-5.3-Flash fits one Spark only as an EXL3 pack (2.05 bpw, 80 GiB).
Verified: `tf-cuda-test exl3` on a GB10: every float64 reference, row and chunk invariance check passes.

